          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Hammurabi's Early Life</strong><br>\nHammurabi was born around 1810 BCE in ancient Mesopotamia. He was the sixth king of the Babylonian dynasty, which rose to prominence under his rule. Not much is known about his early life before becoming king, but it is understood that he was a member of a royal family with a lineage of rulers. His reign began in 1792 BCE and lasted for 42 years, during which he extended Babylon's control over Mesopotamia through military conquests and strategic alliances.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Rise to Power</strong><br>\nAfter ascending to the throne, Hammurabi began consolidating his power within Babylon. He used diplomacy and warfare to subdue neighboring city-states, slowly expanding his kingdom. His leadership was characterized by a strong, centralized administration. He managed to unite the disparate regions of Mesopotamia under his rule, creating one of the earliest and most powerful empires in the ancient world.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Code of Hammurabi</strong><br>\nHammurabi is best known for his set of laws, known as the Code of Hammurabi. This code is one of the oldest deciphered writings of significant length in the world. It was inscribed on a stone stele and placed in a public space so that all citizens could see it. The code contained 282 laws covering a wide range of subjects, including trade, labor, family, and property rights.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
