            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Justice System</strong><br>\nThe laws in the Code of Hammurabi were quite advanced for their time. They included aspects of presumption of innocence and the ability to present evidence. The code also specified different punishments for the rich and poor, and for men and women, highlighting the class divisions of the society. Nevertheless, it aimed to be a guide for the fair and just treatment of all, with the famous phrase \"eye for an eye\" epitomizing its reciprocal justice.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Economy and Trade</strong><br>\nUnder Hammurabi, Babylon became a thriving center for trade. The empire's economy was bolstered by improved agricultural techniques and the expansion of trade routes. Hammurabi's laws facilitated trade by standardizing weights and measures and by establishing rules for business transactions, which helped to stabilize the economy and ensure a measure of fairness in dealings.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Infrastructure Development</strong><br>\nHammurabi also focused on improving the infrastructure of his city. He built and restored temples, walls, and canals, which not only strengthened the city's defenses but also improved irrigation for agriculture. These public works projects employed many people and helped to increase the prosperity of his kingdom.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
